function COMPONENT(request : dval) {
    print("<div class=\"doc-detail-layout\"><main class=\"content doc-page doc-detail\"><h2>6. Strings and HTML</h2><div class=\"doc-section content\"><p>Use strings for text and markup expressions for HTML. Markup escapes ordinary strings before they enter the response.</p><h2>Escape dynamic text</h2><pre><code class=\"language-capy\">function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := &quot;&lt;Ada&gt;&quot;\n    print(&lt;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hello, &lt;?= name ?&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/&gt;, &quot;\\n&quot;)\n}\n</code></pre><p><strong>Output</strong></p><pre><code class=\"language-text\">&lt;p&gt;Hello, &amp;lt;Ada&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n</code></pre><p><code>&lt;?= name ?&gt;</code> selects an encoding from its location. HTML text and quoted attributes escape <code>&amp;</code>, <code>&lt;</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, quotes, and apostrophes.</p><p>Inside a <code>script</code> element, a string becomes one self-contained JavaScript literal. The encoder protects the closing tag and JavaScript line separators. Inside a <code>style</code> element, a string becomes one self-contained CSS literal. Integer and Boolean values remain scalar values. <code>f64</code> interpolation is not supported in these elements.</p><pre><code class=\"language-capy\">function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := string(request.query.name, {fallback: &quot;guest&quot;})\n    print(&lt;&gt;\n        &lt;script&gt;const name = &lt;?= name ?&gt;;&lt;/script&gt;\n        &lt;style&gt;.name::before { content: &lt;?= name ?&gt;; }&lt;/style&gt;\n    &lt;/&gt;)\n}\n</code></pre><p>Script and style interpolation must start at a value boundary. Static source after it can apply an operator or a CSS unit. Do not put interpolation inside an existing string, template literal, or comment. Attribute values must use quotes. Tag and attribute names cannot ")
    print("contain interpolation.</p><p>URL, event-handler, and inline-style attributes use HTML attribute escaping. Validate these values for their application context before interpolation.</p><h2>String literals</h2><p>String literals use double quotes:</p><pre><code class=\"language-capy\">function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var message := &quot;Hello&quot;\n    var line := &quot;first\\nsecond&quot;\n    print(message, &quot; &quot;, line, &quot;\\n&quot;)\n}\n</code></pre><p>The supported escapes include <code>\\n</code>, <code>\\r</code>, <code>\\t</code>, <code>\\&quot;</code>, and <code>\\\\</code>. String positions and lengths count bytes, not Unicode characters.</p><p>Use <code>+</code> to join strings:</p><pre><code class=\"language-capy\">function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := &quot;Ada&quot;\n    var greeting := &quot;Hello, &quot; + name\n    print(greeting, &quot;\\n&quot;)\n}\n</code></pre><p>Use a constructor to convert a scalar when a function does not already accept <code>as string</code>:</p><pre><code class=\"language-capy\">function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var label := &quot;Count: &quot; + string(3)\n    print(label, &quot;\\n&quot;)\n}\n</code></pre><h2>Markup expressions</h2><p>A markup expression starts with <code>&lt;&gt;</code> and ends with <code>&lt;/&gt;</code>:</p><pre><code class=\"language-capy\">function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var title := &quot;Report&quot;\n    print(&lt;&gt;\n        &lt;h1&gt;&lt;?= title ?&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;\n        &lt;p&gt;Ready&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;/&gt;)\n}\n</code></pre><p>The expression has type <code>markup</code>. It is a value. It does not write to the response by itself. Use <code>print(markup_value)</code> to output it. You can also return <code>markup</code> from an ordinary function or insert it into other markup.</p><pre><code")
    print(" class=\"language-capy\">function badge(label : string) markup {\n    -&gt; &lt;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;?= label ?&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/&gt;\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    print(badge(&quot;Ready&quot;))\n}\n</code></pre><p><strong>Output</strong></p><pre><code class=\"language-text\">&lt;strong&gt;Ready&lt;/strong&gt;\n</code></pre><h2>Interpolation rule</h2><p><code>&lt;?= value ?&gt;</code> escapes output at the interpolation site. <code>&lt;?: value ?&gt;</code> emits output without escaping. It works only in HTML text.</p><p>The interpolation form selects escaping. The value type does not.</p><h2>Common string operations</h2><p>Use <code>length</code>, <code>substr</code>, <code>find</code>, <code>contains</code>, <code>replace</code>, <code>lower</code>, <code>upper</code>, <code>split</code>, and <code>join</code> for ordinary text work. Use <code>html_escape</code> when an API needs escaped text instead of a <code>markup</code> value.</p><p>Strings use automatic reference counting. Assignment and function calls preserve their lifetime. Most programs do not need to call <code>clone</code>.</p></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := &quot;&lt;Ada&gt;&quot;\n    print(&lt;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hello, &lt;?= name ?&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/&gt;, &quot;\\n&quot;)\n}\n</pre></div><p><strong>Output</strong></p><div class=\"example-output\"><div class=\"example-output-label\">Output</div><pre>&lt;p&gt;Hello, &amp;lt;Ada&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := string(request.query.name,")
    print(" {fallback: &quot;guest&quot;})\n    print(&lt;&gt;\n        &lt;script&gt;const name = &lt;?= name ?&gt;;&lt;/script&gt;\n        &lt;style&gt;.name::before { content: &lt;?= name ?&gt;; }&lt;/style&gt;\n    &lt;/&gt;)\n}\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var message := &quot;Hello&quot;\n    var line := &quot;first\\nsecond&quot;\n    print(message, &quot; &quot;, line, &quot;\\n&quot;)\n}\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := &quot;Ada&quot;\n    var greeting := &quot;Hello, &quot; + name\n    print(greeting, &quot;\\n&quot;)\n}\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var label := &quot;Count: &quot; + string(3)\n    print(label, &quot;\\n&quot;)\n}\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var title := &quot;Report&quot;\n    print(&lt;&gt;\n        &lt;h1&gt;&lt;?= title ?&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;\n        &lt;p&gt;Ready&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;/&gt;)\n}\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">function badge(label : string) markup {\n    -&gt; &lt;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;?= label ?&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/&gt;\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    print(badge(&quot;Ready&quot;))\n}\n</pre></div><p><strong>Output</strong></p><div cla")
    print("ss=\"example-output\"><div class=\"example-output-label\">Output</div><pre>&lt;strong&gt;Ready&lt;/strong&gt;\n</pre></div></div><nav class=\"guide-navigation\" aria-label=\"Capy guide navigation\"><div class=\"guide-previous\">Previous: <a href=\"/doc/\">Guide index</a></div><div class=\"guide-index\"><a href=\"/doc/\">Guide index</a></div><div class=\"guide-next\">Next: <a href=\"/doc/\">Guide index</a></div></nav></main><aside class=\"doc-section see-also\"><h3>See also</h3><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/type/string/\">string</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/api/html-escape/\">html_escape</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/guide/functions-and-closures/\">5. Functions</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/guide/web-handlers-and-requests/\">9. Handling a web request</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/api/string/\">string</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/api/length/\">length</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/api/clone/\">clone</a></aside></div>")
}
